// Deal or Force - who holds a deterrent no neighbour can afford to test (Deterrence.cs).
//
// A row is a country tag and a tier. Tier 1 is mutual assured destruction: two tier-1
// countries do not fight each other directly, because the war judgement prices such a war
// out of the arithmetic (Defines.AiMutualDeterrencePrice). Higher tiers are reserved for
// mods that want a second rung - a defence that survives a first strike, say - the code
// reads "at least 1" everywhere today.
//
// The club of 2024, as history left it. A mod for an earlier era ships this file empty, or
// without it, and the mechanic never speaks; a mod for a future one adds the rows its
// history wrote. Acquisition in play is a technology with `effects: deterrence`, not a row
// here - rows are who already holds one when the scenario opens.
{
  "holders": {
    "RUS": 1,
    "USA": 1,
    "CHN": 1,
    "FRA": 1,
    "GBR": 1,
    "IND": 1,
    "PAK": 1,
    "PRK": 1,
    "ISR": 1
  }
}
